{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Authored puzzle content, ported from the RAW table in design/Squarebuzz.dc.html.",
    "Grids use '#' for a filled cell and '.' for an empty one, one string per row, so a",
    "puzzle can be read and edited by eye in a diff. Row/column clues are never stored -",
    "they are derived by ClueCalculator, which keeps them impossible to desynchronise",
    "from the solution.",
    "Sizes 15/20/25 have no authored content and are produced by the generator instead.",
    "Authoring rules: 10x10 pictures target 45-65% fill and carry a few anchor runs of 6+",
    "cells; avoid sparse symmetric detail, checkerboards, and long thin diagonals; at most",
    "2 fully-empty rows and 2 fully-empty columns per puzzle. Validate every edit with",
    "`dotnet run tools/validate-puzzles.cs` - all puzzles must solve by pure line logic.",
    "The order of the puzzles array IS the campaign milestone order: easiest first within",
    "each size block (all 5x5 before all 10x10), with 'heart' pinned to position 1."
  ],

